        "parms": "# && || & | << >> — logic and bits\n&& and || are logical: any number other than 0 counts as true, and they send 1 or 0. & | << and >> work on the bits of whole numbers, and send an int; a float is truncated first. As in arithmetic, the left inlet is hot and the right inlet cold.\nMax's versions work the same way, except that Max's left inlet also works out again on a bang. Here a bang does nothing.",
