        "parms": "1. Flip the two toggles. && sends 1 only while both are on, || while either is. The right toggle goes through trigger b i, which stores it on the right and then bangs the left box, so both toggles answer at once.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 35": {
        "ID": 35,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "310.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "2. Bits. 12 is 1100 in binary and 10 is 1010. Click 12: & keeps the bits both have, 1000, which is 8. | keeps the bits either has, 1110, which is 14.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 36": {
        "ID": 36,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "420.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "3. Shifting left by 1 doubles a whole number, shifting right halves it and drops the remainder. Click 6: 12 and 3. Click -8: >> keeps the sign, -4.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 37": {
        "ID": 37,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "530.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "4. Bit-packing. Two numbers from 0 to 15 fit in one: the high one shifted left by 4, OR the low one. Click 2 and then 5: 2 × 16 + 5 = 37. Click 9, then 15.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 38": {
        "ID": 38,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "640.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "5. Unpacking: >> 4 brings the high number back, & 15 keeps the low four bits. Both come out as they went in.",
